---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Project One" description="A clean Astro build focused on performance and sharp UI details.">
  <section class="max-w-2xl">
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm tracking-wide text-text-light">
      <a href="/projects" class="hover:text-primary">← Projects</a>
    </p>
    <h1 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-black text-text-dark md:text-5xl">Project One</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-text-light">A clean Astro build focused on performance and sharp UI details.</p>

    <img
      src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1498050108023-c5249f4df085?w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"
      alt="Project One"
      width="1200"
      height="630"
      class="mb-10 w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
      loading="eager"
    />

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-text-light">
      Project One is a lean Astro site built to prove that great performance and sharp design don't require a heavy
      framework. The goal was a sub-second load on mobile with a Lighthouse score above 95 across all four categories.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-10 text-text-light">
      Every component was built from scratch — no UI library, no unnecessary dependencies. Layout, typography, and
      colour choices were driven by the content rather than a template.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">What I built</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-text-light">
      A fully static site with a custom design system defined in Tailwind config. Responsive grid layouts, accessible
      navigation with a mobile overlay, and a structured content model that makes future updates straightforward.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-10 text-text-light">
      Deployment is handled via GitHub Actions pushing to GitHub Pages — zero server cost, instant global CDN, and
      automated rebuilds on every commit to main.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">Tech stack</h2>
    <ul class="mb-10 list-disc pl-5 text-text-light space-y-1">
      <li>Astro</li>
      <li>Tailwind CSS</li>
      <li>TypeScript</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
